 "issue": "2026-08-18 (issue #6)",
 "issue_note": "one-day window (531 items, 08-18 04:31 -> 23:44): the window starts at issue #5's PULL, not its cutoff, so the 228 in-scope items of 08-18 00:00-04:31 fall in every full-pool cell and in no issue's window cells, ever. Window-only cells are comparable in KIND to issue #4's one-day window (968 items) and NOT to issue #5's three-day window; they cover 70% of their day where #4's covered 97%, and at 531 items they carry wider bands than #4's. Two instruments changed this issue: the fixed-horizon permeability control gained a membership decomposition and a per-cohort trend test (weather_permeability_control.py), and the GPU stage gained an allocation label-coverage audit that diffs the emitted daily series against the previous PUBLISHED issue (weather_gpu.py). The second found a real retro-movement channel; see allocation_label_audit.",
