 "caveats": [
  "cutoff 2026-08-19T00:00:00Z on all analyses, strictly exclusive; the pull ran 2.9 h after it and the last in-scope item is 08-18 23:44:28, so no in-scope day is partial. 08-18 cells are labelled provisional as standing discipline.",
  "ONE-DAY WINDOW (531 items): window-only cells are comparable in kind to issue #4's one-day window and NOT to issue #5's three-day window. #4's window held 968 items against this one's 531, so #6's window bands are wider; read the narrowing off the full-pool column.",
  "no newcomer cells this issue: 42 newcomer items is below both standing floors (m>=100 Vendi, m>=50 NN). Nothing is claimed about newcomer refresh either way.",
  "delta pipeline: claims and allocation labels cached by kind:id; 759 items claimified this issue and 0 cache evictions for edits (0 edited items across 11,970 compared).",
  "ALLOCATION LABELS RETRO-MOVE: an unparseable classifier answer caches nothing and is retried next issue, so a published day can shift when a retry succeeds. This issue exactly one did - 08-16 went 0.4726 -> 0.4720 (one item, labelled WORLD, on a 786-item day). The channel is now audited every issue (allocation_trend.label_audit); label coverage is 12,429/12,501 (99.4%).",
  "THE label_audit BLOCK DESCRIBES A LATER PASS. This issue's delta pass classified 825 items (759 new + 66 retries) and resolved 1 retry, leaving 65 persistent published-day failures + 7 first-attempt 08-18 failures = 72 uncovered. The published block was emitted by a warm-cache verification pass, so its delta_classified=72 is that pass's count, not the issue's. weather_gpu.py now stamps each audit with pass_type; this issue's artifact predates that field.",
  "ACCUMULATION STATISTICS: the rolling halves, the pooled dip share and (until this issue) the fixed-horizon permeability mean all average over history that grows each issue. Where an issue-local equivalent exists it is now the primary reading. Every per-issue decomposition here depends on the shared prefix not moving, which is asserted rather than assumed.",
  "single-normalizer / bge-only: rolling series and newcomer cells are Qwen-normalized and bge-embedded; the three-embedder check covers placement only.",
  "allocation LEVEL carries the parent study's 0.31-0.71 specification range; kappa(Qwen,Gemma) = 0.4278 on the agent pool. The TREND is the cleaner object.",
  "the lemmy.world reference is FROZEN (2023-06 founding month, 55,223 items) and read from results/lemmy_baseline/results.json; never re-measured per issue. Its platform share is 0.4665 [0.4515, 0.4853] author-clustered - a point estimate with a band, not a threshold.",
  "the lemmy frame is 55.7% meta-tier with c/lemmyworld alone 41.7%, a property of the pre-arrival cohort that over-weights meta and makes the human benchmark MORE self-referential; direction known, magnitude not (baseline s2).",
  "the fixed-span churn control still averages over a cohort set whose membership grows each issue; it removes the observation-length confound, not the membership one. The fixed-horizon permeability control now has that membership term measured rather than assumed.",
  "core_n is retired as a series (issue #5); the fixed-horizon permeability RUNNING MEAN is retired as a behavioural series this issue - it is a composition statistic by construction.",
  "the per-cohort trend test is three correlated horizons of one hypothesis; only N=3 reaches nominal significance and no multiplicity correction is applied, so it is read as direction, not as an established effect.",
